A-08 Wi-Fi result handler, A/B on the zxing_api36 emulator (Android 16), 2026-11-02

Driven as a real scan, not a replay: a WIFI: QR code was generated with this fork's
:core, put on the emulator's virtual-scene wall with
  adb -s emulator-5556 emu virtualscene-image wall <png>
and the app decoded it off the camera. The code has to be small enough on the poster
to fit inside the viewfinder -- a 600 px code on an 800 px canvas is clipped by the
frame and never decodes; 420 px on a 1400 px canvas works.

DN-ENG41 could not be used for this: its camera cannot be aimed from the command
line, and replaying a Wi-Fi row from history does not leave the result on screen
long enough to press the button -- CaptureActivity.onResume resets the status view
after onActivityResult has handled it. That is a separate oddity, not A-08.

== BEFORE, scanning WIFI:S:A08TestNet;T:WPA;P:supersecret123;; ==
  the result screen offers "Connect to Network", the toast says
  "Requesting connection to network...", and then:

    W WifiConfigManager: Unable to add network "A08TestNet"

  Nothing else happens. That is the whole of defect A-08: addNetwork returns -1 for a
  non-system app from Android 10 on, and the UI had already claimed success.

== AFTER, the same barcode ==
  Pressing the button starts com.android.settings/.wifi.addappnetworks.
  AddAppNetworksActivity, which asks "Save this network? A08TestNet" with Cancel and
  Save. Pressing Save:

    V WifiConfigManager: Adding/Updating network A08TestNet          (system, uid 1000)
    D WifiConfigManager: Enable disabled network: "A08TestNet" num=0
    D WifiClientModeImpl: ConnectableState ... "A08TestNet"WPA_PSK nid=1

  and the network is saved:

    $ adb shell cmd wifi list-networks
    Network Id      SSID                         Security type
    0            AndroidWifi                      open
    1            A08TestNet                       wpa2-psk

  No toast on this path: the system dialog is the feedback, and a toast saying a
  connection was requested would be the same lie as before, only earlier.

== AFTER, WIFI:S:A08WepNet;T:WEP;P:abcdef1234;; ==
  WEP has no equivalent in the network suggestion API, so it is reported rather than
  silently dropped:

    W WifiNetworkAdder: WEP cannot be expressed as a network suggestion

  and the toast reads "Android can no longer add WEP networks. Add it by hand in
  Wi-Fi settings." Screenshot: reports/a08-wep-unsupported-api36.png

== What is not verified ==
  The Android 10 route (addNetworkSuggestions) and the pre-Android-10 route (the old
  WifiConfiguration path, kept because minSdk is 21). No device or emulator running
  either version is available here. The branch that selects them is a plain
  Build.VERSION.SDK_INT check; the code they run is not.

  ACTION_WIFI_ADD_NETWORKS resolves on both machines that are available --
  com.android.settings.wifi.addappnetworks.AddAppNetworksActivity on DN-ENG41 as well
  as on the emulator -- so the ActivityNotFoundException fallback is also untested.
